# How long each layer's demand survives being unanswered, or the typed reason nobody knows. One
# row per layer: the span a queued order stays an order.
#
# The half of the time axis the schema filed as missing
#   `pm:Divisibility` sits on `Nameplate`, so `window` is the supply's duty cycle, and its own
#   annotation says the mirror, demand with a lifetime, is a fact about demand and names
#   `Layer/timeSlack` as where it would go "if demand ever gains structure". `pm:Demand/patience`
#   is that structure, and this relation is the half of the axis it makes askable.
#
# A patience is not a time slack
#   The units are how you tell. A slack is quoted in the unit of the shares it bounds
#   (`slack_unit_mismatch` requires it), and a patience is a span of time that bounds no shares.
#   `merge-holding-composition`'s `shift-line` files both and they carry the same numbers in
#   different units, because that layer's unit is service time, so the wait and the queue ahead of
#   you are one quantity. The document argues exactly that in a comment. It is a fact about that
#   layer and not a licence to fold the two.
#
# The range and its licence are two relations
#   A shop knows the impatient customer leaves at three minutes and the last at ten; that is the
#   claim. "Service within five minutes" is a negotiated edge on it, and `boundOrigin` is where an
#   edge says whose it is. Reading the two together is the difference between renegotiating a
#   term and measuring again. The edge's owner is the patience claim's own, in
#   epistemics/claims.sqlc where `owns` is `pm:demand/pm:patience`, beside every other claim's.
#
# Zero patience is a claim of zero
#   Never `absent/reason = none`. Demand that leaves the moment it is not served has a patience of
#   zero, and a measured zero is a claim: `patience` is a `pm:StatedClaim`, whose absent arm
#   carries `pm:ClaimAbsenceReason`, and that type has no `none`. So `patience_absent` can
#   honestly hold three reasons and not four. The validator refuses the fourth and
#   `a_patience_absence_has_no_none` refuses it again on the way in.
#
# The spelling it replaces
#   That spelling is why the element exists. `merge-group-composition`'s `on-call` layer "does not
#   survive being held at all", and with no patience element that fact has nowhere to go but the
#   time slack's `absent/reason = none`, which is a different claim. It is a `timeSlack` of
#   [0, 0, 0] and a patience beside it. Its patience is `unmeasured`, and the gap between the two
#   is worth a query: a slack of zero is a buffer nobody funded, a patience of zero is demand that
#   would not use one even if somebody did.
-- pm:Demand/pm:patience, beside the demand it qualifies.
SELECT l.filing, l.layer,
       l.patience_low, l.patience_mode, l.patience_high, l.patience_unit,
       l.patience_absent,
       l.demand_unit
FROM pm.layer l
